    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm planning a big gala for a law firm (about 500 people) and we just got a bunch of last minute updates. We have quite a few guests with severe nut allergies and a significant number of vegan requests. What's the best way to communicate these specifics to the kitchen staff so nothing gets mixed up, and how should we handle the labeling on the buffet line to keep everyone safe?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, send an urgent message to the kitchen staff detailing the nut allergies and vegan requests. Use a shared digital platform to ensure everyone can view the changes in real time. Label all buffet items clearly, using a separate color-coded system—for example, red for nut-free, green for vegan, and including a note about potential cross-contamination risks. Consider placing these details in prominent spots orders of the day, on the menu, and at the beginning of each food station. Follow up with all catering staff, then send a final reminder the night before the gala. It might also help to have a Command Center set up to handle any requests from the guests directly.",
